From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:41:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] feat(ui): phones get the reviewer layout, review first
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With FULL_UI off, desktop and the embedded panel already used the reviewer
layout: one dock along the bottom, the Hand first, Layers folded, the
right-hand panel closed. Phones still had the editor's own phone layout: a top
bar, a tool strip along the bottom, Comments/AI tabs and an actions sheet that
led with Layers and Prototype mode. A reviewer on a phone saw an editor.

Now a phone (<= 900px, FULL_UI off, floating panels) gets the same layout,
sized for a thumb, as bottom toolbars on phones usually are (iOS HIG tab and
toolbars, the Figma and Miro mobile viewers): one dock at the bottom edge,
above the safe area, with
  back to the canvases, Hand, Comment, the tool list | Comments, Pages and
  layers, ••• (the canvas actions sheet)
at the 40px touch size. It fits a 320px screen: 283px wide, 295px with a
tool picked from the list, because on a phone that tool takes the list's
button instead of adding one; Prototype mode stays in the list and AI
activity is a tab of the Comments sheet. No top bar; the zoom pill floats
above the dock and Present sits top right. The stage keeps the dock's 66px
clear at the bottom.

The ••• sheet carries the canvas's name as its title and what the desktop
dock holds besides: import, share, export, Connect AI, your display name and
settings, each only for whoever may use it. The Pages and layers sheet opens
with Layers folded, as the desktop panel does. Guests and share-link
visitors get no back button and no panel button, as on desktop.

FULL_UI on (or doop:full-ui in localStorage) keeps the old phone layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
